{"id":"465d89be-64f1-4f71-8f43-21cfed34623c","recipient":"ef440df2-a098-44c4-b54d-aa1af299148e","sender":"ad04e811-7db2-40d5-8256-652d5475fdc0","priority":"MESSAGE_PRIORITY_HIGH","timestamp":"2026-09-01T20:02:50.715487700Z","renderDetails":{"messageTitle":"Message from Channel Data Analyst Gamma (research)"},"content":"Here is the highly structured, data-dense comparison between NexLev and vidIQ data for the 3 specified channels:\n\n### 1. Vericade\n\n| Metric | NexLev Data | vidIQ Data |\n|---|---|---|\n| **30-Day Views** | 1.41M (95K long, 1.3M shorts) | ~8M views/month |\n| **Monthly Revenue** | $548 | $14,400.00 |\n| **RPM** | $5.18 (Long-form) / ~$0.39 (Blended) | $1.80 (Blended) |\n| **Tier 1 Geo %** | 81.5% | 68% |\n| **Lifetime Earnings** | ~$30,500 | $140,912.05 |\n\n*Note: NexLev attributes Vericade's low monthly revenue to their shift to Shorts ($0.041 RPM) whereas vidIQ estimates significantly higher blended RPM and shorts view volume.*\n\n### 2. Just Explained\n\n| Metric | NexLev Data | vidIQ Data |\n|---|---|---|\n| **30-Day Views** | 2.23M views/month | ~800K views/month |\n| **Monthly Revenue** | $13,118 | $4,400.00 |\n| **RPM** | $6.07 | $5.50 |\n| **Tier 1 Geo %** | 35.3% (US 30.9% + UK 4.4%)* | 85% (UK/US heavy) |\n| **Lifetime Earnings** | ~$19,660 | $19,138.32 |\n\n*\\* NexLev also notes additional traffic from Germany (5.4%) which brings up CPMs despite lower US concentration.*\n\n### 3. The Cosmic Explainer\n\n| Metric | NexLev Data | vidIQ Data |\n|---|---|---|\n| **30-Day Views** | 5,585 views/month | ~55K views/month |\n| **Monthly Revenue** | $28 | $247.50 |\n| **RPM** | $5.17 | $4.50 |\n| **Tier 1 Geo %** | 79.5% (US+UK+CA+AU) | 72% |\n| **Lifetime Earnings** | ~$13,524 | $11,767.10 |\n\n*Note: Both platforms recognize this channel is inactive, but NexLev pegs the current long-tail views (5.5K) significantly lower than vidIQ's estimate (55K).*","sourceMetadata":{"tool":{"conversationId":"ad04e811-7db2-40d5-8256-652d5475fdc0","stepIndex":